+# ---- Profile-provided trampolines (CAVES of the patch file) ----
+# Some games have a bug in their own code that only this platform meets: a handle table slot they freed is dereferenced
+# again without a check, so the game dies on a null pointer where a console would read stale memory. The fix belongs at
+# that instruction, but a module's text segment has no spare bytes to hold it (a stripped Unity main is packed solid).
+# A cave is therefore emitted into the patch area -- which the loader maps executable right beside the module -- and the
+# site keeps a branch to it. Entries: (offset in the image, the 4 original bytes as hex, the replacement's words as hex,
+# reason); the words are machine code for the module, and the branch to the cave is written by this script.
+for _off, _ob, _words, _why in PATCHES['CAVES'].get(BUILD_ID, []):
